  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Humanitarian response to regions affected by floods and extreme weather conditions in Bolivia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Excessive rains and extreme weather conditions have caused severe flooding in the Amazon region of northern  Bolivia. CAFOD&#x2019;s church partner, CEPAS Caritas is responding with the support of a number of Caritas agencies to this emergency with a three-phased project covering a six-month period. The severity of the flooding has meant that very little information about the needs of the communities is coming out of the region as travel is nearly impossible. The project will begin by focusing on provision of food and household kits. The second phase will concentrate on food security, water, hygiene and improving shelter. The final phase will focus on rehabilitation and reconstruction.</narrative>
  </description>
